    'natal:ruler9|house|1': 'The 9th house ruler in the Ascendant places philosophy, expansion, and the search for meaning at the heart of personal identity. You tend to present yourself as someone with a broad vision, curious about the world and inclined to explore experiences that expand your horizons.',
    'natal:ruler9|house|10': 'With the 9th house ruler in the 10th house, the career may be linked to teaching, publishing, law, religion, or international work. A reputation built on genuine knowledge and ethical principles tends to be lasting and meaningful.',
    'natal:ruler9|house|11': 'The 9th house ruler in the 11th house indicates that groups, networks, and friendships may be sources of philosophical expansion and new perspectives. Humanitarian causes, ideological movements, or learning communities tend to be part of the path.',
    'natal:ruler9|house|12': 'With the 9th house ruler in the 12th house, the spiritual quest and philosophical development may occur in a quiet and inward way. Retreats, introspective studies, or contemplative practices may be especially nourishing for personal growth.',
    'natal:ruler9|house|2': 'With the 9th house ruler in the 2nd house, material growth may be tied to intellectual activities, publishing, teaching, or connections with foreign markets. An open perspective and willingness to keep learning tend to translate into concrete growth opportunities.',
    'natal:ruler9|house|3': 'The 9th house ruler in the 3rd house suggests that a curious mind and philosophical inclination express themselves through communication and everyday learning. There is a potential for connecting ideas from distinct cultures and translating complex knowledge in accessible ways.',
    'natal:ruler9|house|4': 'With the 9th house ruler in the 4th house, emotional identity may be linked to a specific family culture, religion, or philosophy. Finding a second home in another region of the world or integrating diverse traditions in the domestic environment may be part of the path.',
    'natal:ruler9|house|5': 'The 9th house ruler in the 5th house points to a creative life enriched by travel, diverse cultures, and the search for meaning. Romances with people from other countries or the creation of works that explore universal themes may be landmark experiences.',
    'natal:ruler9|house|6': 'With the 9th house ruler in the 6th house, work may involve travel, teaching, holistic healthcare, or services provided to international audiences. There is also an invitation to pay attention to how the mind and beliefs influence physical health.',
    'natal:ruler9|house|7': 'The 9th house ruler in the 7th house suggests that partnerships with people from different cultures or worldviews may be especially enriching. Relationships that expand perspective and stimulate philosophical growth tend to be the most meaningful.',
    'natal:ruler9|house|8': 'With the 9th house ruler in the 8th house, the spiritual and philosophical quest has a dimension of depth and transformation. There is an attraction to investigating the mysteries of existence, and periods of crisis may become portals to a broader understanding of life.',
    'natal:ruler9|house|9': 'The 9th house ruler in its own house highlights philosophy, religion, travel, and higher studies as central themes of life. There is a natural inclination to continually expand horizons and to connect personal experiences to a broader worldview.',
